# Report cards (ChatGPT / audit)

When delivering a **report card** (audit summaries, phase reviews, status for ChatGPT):

1. **Foldable** — wrap the card in HTML `<details>` / `<summary>` so the user can collapse it.
2. **Copy-friendly** — put the card body in a single fenced code block inside `<details>` so Cursor shows the copy icon on the block.
3. **Dark theme** — use a black/dark wrapper; light text in the summary line.

## Template

<details style="background:#0a0a0a;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:8px;padding:0;margin:12px 0;">
<summary style="cursor:pointer;padding:10px 14px;color:#fbbf24;font-weight:600;list-style:none;">📋 Copy report card — [TITLE]</summary>

<div style="background:#111;padding:8px 12px 12px;border-top:1px solid #2a2a2a;">

```
[PASTE FULL CARD HERE — one block only]
```

</div>
</details>

## Rules

- One report card per deliverable unless the user asks for more.
- Summary line: short title + what the card is for (e.g. "Phase 10J audit").
- Card interior: keep the existing box-drawing / section layout inside the code fence.
- Do **not** nest multiple code fences inside the card body.
- Command cards (git/shell steps) still follow `command-cards.mdc` — separate blocks, not merged into report cards unless the card is command-only.
